01:36:38.320 --> 01:36:42.810
[INAUDIBLE] What is the
difference between this and the

01:36:42.810 --> 01:36:43.760
[INAUDIBLE].

01:36:46.790 --> 01:36:48.980
Well, and that's
where the engineering

01:36:48.980 --> 01:36:53.330
tries to connect with the
art and the architecture.

01:36:53.330 --> 01:36:56.360
So the code doesn't
know about aesthetics.

01:36:56.360 --> 01:36:58.670
It just tells us what
is the most efficient.

01:36:58.670 --> 01:37:01.700
But what it can also do is
it can tell us how well we

01:37:01.700 --> 01:37:03.090
do with anything else.

01:37:03.090 --> 01:37:05.750
So we actually
purposefully developed

01:37:05.750 --> 01:37:07.970
a sort of a way for
the architectures

01:37:07.970 --> 01:37:10.902
to put their designs
directly into our code

01:37:10.902 --> 01:37:12.110
and see how far off they are.

01:37:12.110 --> 01:37:13.610
And it's very interesting
